#!/bin/bash
# The referee.
#
# One rule, enforced mechanically, on every agent including the one that wrote
# it: a commit must say who made it.
#
# Written after the Control Room reported "Codex 42, Claude 31" when 26 of those
# commits were Claude's own, unsigned. Attribution by subtraction invented an
# author, and the number that was wrong was the one everybody was reading.
#
# A referee does not judge quality. It enforces a rule nobody can bend, and it
# is the only fair way to enforce one, because the player who wrote the rule is
# the player most likely to forget it. That is exactly what happened.
#
# Install:  git config core.hooksPath scripts/hooks

MSG_FILE="$1"
[ -f "$MSG_FILE" ] || exit 0

# Merge, revert, squash and fixup messages are generated by git itself.
head -1 "$MSG_FILE" | grep -qE '^(Merge|Revert|fixup!|squash!)' && exit 0

if grep -qiE '^(Sal0-From|Co-Authored-By):' "$MSG_FILE"; then
  exit 0
fi

cat >&2 <<'WHISTLE'

  ── WHISTLE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Unsigned commit. Every commit must name who made it.

  Add ONE of these as the last line:

    Sal0-From: SAL0-01                              (Codex)
    Sal0-From: SAL0-04                              (Claude)
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

  Why this is enforced rather than asked for: the Control Room read
  "Codex 42, Claude 31" while 26 of those commits were Claude's own,
  unsigned. Attribution by subtraction invented an author, and every
  decision made from that board was made from a wrong number.

  The agent who wrote this rule is the one who broke it. That is why
  a referee exists instead of an honour system.

  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

WHISTLE
exit 1
